# No em dashes on guest pages

Do **not** place em dashes (`—` U+2014) or en dashes (`–` U+2013) in guest-facing copy under `public/`.

## Guest surfaces

Includes (not limited to):

- Cert homes (`comptia-sec+-home.html`, and other `*-home.html`)
- About, verify, discounts, sample landings
- `public/secplus/`, `COMP_TIA_SEC+/SEC+_Samples/`
- Guest JS that injects visible strings (promo banners, sample nav, conversion copy)

## Use instead

| Avoid | Prefer |
|-------|--------|
| `Tier A sources—not dumps` | `Tier A sources - not dumps` or rephrase with a comma/period |
| `Research First — Not AI` | `Research First: Not AI` or `Research First - Not AI` |
| `August — claim it` | `August - claim it` |

ASCII hyphen-minus (`-`) or normal punctuation only. Do not use `—` or `–` in HTML text, `aria-label`, JSON-LD, meta descriptions, or JS string literals shown to guests.
